Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.964 --> 00:00:04.338
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:10.210
SPEAKER: Click the
Activate Google Cloud Shell

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:13.250
button at the top right
of the console window.

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:16.230
A Cloud Shell session
opens inside a new frame

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:18.510
at the bottom of the
console, and displays

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:20.250
a command line prompt.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:23.220
It may take a few
seconds to initialize.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:25.980
Once your Cloud Shell
session is ready to use,

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:28.080
you can do things like
go to your home directory

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:31.710
and use VI to view your
bashrc configuration.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:34.180
In this Quick Start,
we'll preview and deploy

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.120
an App Engine application.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.550
First, clone the
sample app, and run

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:41.190
it locally in the
Cloud Shell session

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:44.830
using the App Engine
development server.

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:46.780
Click the Web Preview
button, and then

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:50.200
select the port number
from the displayed menu.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.300
Cloud Shell opens
the preview URL

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:56.280
at its proxy service in
a new browser window.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:59.370
When you are done previewing
the App Engine app,

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:03.480
type Control-C to stop
the development server.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:05.730
Now that we've
previewed our app,

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:10.260
we can deploy our App Engine
app using gcloud app deploy.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:13.240
This may take a few
minutes to complete.

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:17.070
Once deployed, you can open your
application in the web browser.

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:23.160
The URL is at your project
ID dot appspot.com.

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:26.010
Now, if the application has
not yet finished deploying,

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:28.860
you'll see an error
message in the web browser.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:33.610
Simply wait until deployment is
finished, and refresh the page.

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:34.900
Congratulations.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:37.150
You've successfully
previewed and deployed

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:40.420
an App Engine app using
just your browser thanks

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:42.710
to the power of Cloud Shell.

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:46.060
[MUSIC PLAYING]

